    historyContent: {
      origins: "Developed in the early 2000s in Las Vegas and California card rooms as part of the 'Mixed Game' movement. It was created to merge the popularity of Badugi with the more established Ace-to-Five Lowball format.",
      originCountries: [
        'United States',
      ],
      timeline: [
        '2004: Badugi gains popularity in North American poker rooms.',
        "2008: Badacey emerges as a staple in 'H.O.R.S.E.'-style mixed games.",
        "Present: Frequently played in the World Series of Poker (WSOP) dealer's choice events.",
      ],
      evolution: "The game was designed to reduce the 'luck' factor of single-pot Lowball by forcing players to manage two different ranking systems simultaneously.",
      cultural: "Known as a 'Thinker's Game', often played with blinds and a fixed-limit betting structure.",
    },
    setupContent: {
      players: 'Two to six players. All players post an ante; the dealer gives each player five cards face down. Play uses a dealer button with small and big blinds; the game is commonly played with fixed-limit betting in card rooms.',
