          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win half the pot with the best 4-card Badugi and half with the best 5-card Ace-to-Five low.',
          gameplay: '1. **Blinds**: Players post small and big blinds. 2. **Deal**: 5 cards each. 3. **Betting Round 1**. 4. **First Draw**: Players discard and draw. 5. **Betting Round 2**. 6. **Second Draw**. 7. **Betting Round 3**. 8. **Third Draw**. 9. **Final Betting Round**. 10. **Showdown**: Split pot.',
          keyRules: [
            'A 3-card Badugi loses to any 4-card Badugi.',
            'In the Lowball half, if you have a pair, your low is disqualified from the top ranks.',
            'A-2-3-4-5 is the best low; A-2-3-4 (rainbow) is the best Badugi.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize the Lowball half first. A solid A-2-3-4-5 low will almost always guarantee you a 4-card Badugi attempt. It is much easier to scoop with a strong low.',
          intermediate: "Draw heavy early. If you don't have three cards to a good low or Badugi, discard all five cards in the first round. Don't fall in love with a King-high Badugi.",
          advanced: 'Snowing: A bluffing technique where you stand pat (draw zero cards) as if you have a perfect hand, forcing opponents to fold their drawing hands even if you actually have nothing.',
          tips: [
            'Aces represent double value in Badacey: they are the best card for both the Low and the Badugi halves.',
            "Pay attention to 'folded' cards if the game allows peeking at the muck; it tells you which low cards are out of play.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
